{"id": "JAH-FOG-ARCH-000003", "slug": "fog-computing-architecture", "title": "Fog Computing Architecture \u2014 Core concepts", "edition": "public", "src": "public-harvest", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "fog data science database record", "ladder_rank": 5, "body": "Public edition. Public fog data science knowledge, fact-checked reference. Core concepts: three-tier fog model; fog node; fog cluster; northbound/southbound interfaces; fog gateway; fog-to-cloud federation; hierarchical fog; peer fog collaboration; fog orchestrator; device-fog-cloud continuum.", "concepts": ["three-tier fog model", "fog node", "fog cluster", "northbound/southbound interfaces", "fog gateway", "fog-to-cloud federation", "hierarchical fog", "peer fog collaboration", "fog orchestrator", "device-fog-cloud continuum"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Core operation executed", "code": "// core: greedy scheduler assigns tasks to the lowest-rtt node with free cpu\nconst order=[...T.tasks].sort((a,b)=>b.cpu-a.cpu);\nconst load={};const assign={};\nfor(const tk of order){const cand=T.nodes.filter(n=>(load[n.id]||0)+tk.cpu<=n.cpu).sort((a,b)=>a.rtt_ms-b.rtt_ms);assert(cand.length>0,'no node for '+tk.id);const n=cand[0];load[n.id]=(load[n.id]||0)+tk.cpu;assign[tk.id]=n.id;}\nconst lat=Math.max(...Object.keys(assign).map(tid=>{const n=T.nodes.find(x=>x.id===assign[tid]);const t=T.tasks.find(x=>x.id===tid);return n.rtt_ms+t.ms;}));\nJ({assign,total_latency_ms:lat,cloud_rtt_ms:T.cloud_rtt_ms,faster_than_cloud:T.cloud_rtt_ms-lat});assert(lat<T.cloud_rtt_ms,'fog wins');", "verified_output": "{\"assign\":{\"t2\":\"fog-1\",\"t4\":\"fog-2\",\"t1\":\"fog-1\",\"t3\":\"fog-2\"},\"total_latency_ms\":13,\"cloud_rtt_ms\":120,\"faster_than_cloud\":107}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_order": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt item 89 (fog data science)", "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 8, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "JAH Fog Computing Architecture Librarian", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["fog-nodes-orchestration", "fog-vs-cloud-vs-edge", "fog-data-lifecycle", "fog-data-science-master"], "sibling_edition": "fog-computing-architecture-signature"}}
{"id": "JAH-FOG-ARCH-000004", "slug": "fog-computing-architecture", "title": "Fog Computing Architecture \u2014 Worked example", "edition": "public", "src": "public-harvest", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "fog data science database record", "ladder_rank": 7, "body": "Public edition. Public fog data science knowledge, fact-checked reference. A smart-factory deployment: vibration sensors (device tier) stream to shop-floor gateways (fog tier) that aggregate and filter; only anomalies and hourly summaries ascend to the cloud (cloud tier) for fleet-wide model retraining.", "concepts": ["three-tier fog model", "fog node", "fog cluster", "northbound/southbound interfaces", "fog gateway", "fog-to-cloud federation", "hierarchical fog", "peer fog collaboration", "fog orchestrator", "device-fog-cloud continuum"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Worked example end to end", "code": "// end-to-end: vibration samples -> fog filter -> anomaly flag\nconst samples=[0.2,0.3,0.25,0.28,0.31,0.9,1.2,0.29,0.26];const mean=samples.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0)/samples.length;\nconst anom=samples.filter(s=>s>2*mean);const sent_up=anom.length+1;\nJ({samples:samples.length,mean:+mean.toFixed(3),anomalies:anom.length,sent_to_cloud:sent_up,reduction_pct:Math.round(100*(1-sent_up/samples.length))});assert(anom.length===2,'anomalies');", "verified_output": "{\"samples\":9,\"mean\":0.443,\"anomalies\":2,\"sent_to_cloud\":3,\"reduction_pct\":67}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_order": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt item 89 (fog data science)", "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 8, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "JAH Fog Computing Architecture Librarian", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["fog-nodes-orchestration", "fog-vs-cloud-vs-edge", "fog-data-lifecycle", "fog-data-science-master"], "sibling_edition": "fog-computing-architecture-signature"}}
{"id": "JAH-FOG-ARCH-000005", "slug": "fog-computing-architecture", "title": "Fog Computing Architecture \u2014 Safety, limits, and failure modes", "edition": "public", "src": "public-harvest", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "fog data science database record", "ladder_rank": 9, "body": "Public edition. Public fog data science knowledge, fact-checked reference. Fog nodes are resource-constrained relative to cloud servers; the architecture trades raw compute for proximity. Single fog node failure can island devices behind it unless failover peers exist.", "concepts": ["three-tier fog model", "fog node", "fog cluster", "northbound/southbound interfaces", "fog gateway", "fog-to-cloud federation", "hierarchical fog", "peer fog collaboration", "fog orchestrator", "device-fog-cloud continuum"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Safety limits enforced", "code": "const CAP=10n**15n;const request=1000n;const over=CAP+1n;const ok1=request<=CAP;const ok2=over<=CAP;const node={cpu:8,used:7};const job={cpu:4};const fits=node.used+job.cpu<=node.cpu;J({generator_cap:'10^15 (one quadrillion)',request_ok:ok1,over_cap_refused:!ok2,oversized_job_refused:!fits});assert(ok1&&!ok2&&!fits,'limits');", "verified_output": "{\"generator_cap\":\"10^15 (one quadrillion)\",\"request_ok\":true,\"over_cap_refused\":true,\"oversized_job_refused\":true}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_order": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt item 89 (fog data science)", "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 8, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "JAH Fog Computing Architecture Librarian", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["fog-nodes-orchestration", "fog-vs-cloud-vs-edge", "fog-data-lifecycle", "fog-data-science-master"], "sibling_edition": "fog-computing-architecture-signature"}}
{"id": "JAH-FOG-ARCH-000006", "slug": "fog-computing-architecture", "title": "Fog Computing Architecture \u2014 Beginner teaching exercise", "edition": "public", "src": "public-harvest", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "fog data science database record", "ladder_rank": 2, "body": "Public edition. Public fog data science knowledge, fact-checked reference. Start simple: define the fog computing stack (device, fog, cloud tiers) for Fog Computing Architecture, identify which tier each workload belongs on, and verify with a small latency-budget calculation before scaling up.", "concepts": ["three-tier fog model", "fog node", "fog cluster", "northbound/southbound interfaces", "fog gateway", "fog-to-cloud federation", "hierarchical fog", "peer fog collaboration", "fog orchestrator", "device-fog-cloud continuum"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Beginner teaching exercise: cloud vs fog round trip", "code": "const fog=T.nodes[0].rtt_ms;const cloud=T.cloud_rtt_ms;const saved=cloud-fog;const pct=Math.round(100*saved/cloud);J({fog_rtt_ms:fog,cloud_rtt_ms:cloud,saved_ms:saved,saving_pct:pct});assert(saved>0,'saves');assert(pct>50,'big win');", "verified_output": "{\"fog_rtt_ms\":5,\"cloud_rtt_ms\":120,\"saved_ms\":115,\"saving_pct\":96}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_order": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt item 89 (fog data science)", "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 8, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "JAH Fog Computing Architecture Librarian", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["fog-nodes-orchestration", "fog-vs-cloud-vs-edge", "fog-data-li